From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] FT: configure the PTK before marking the STA authorized in the driver

After a successful FT (re)association handle_assoc_cb() marked the
station authorized and pushed the STA flags to the driver first, and
only then let the RSN authenticator retry the PTK configuration that
could not be completed during FT authentication (WPA_ASSOC_FT). After
the 4-way handshake the order is the opposite: the PTK is configured
and only then is the station authorized.

With an AP MLD and a non-AP MLD on ath12k this order mattered: the
station was authorized on all links before any pairwise key existed and
the data path stayed dead after the FT roam. Configure the PTK before
hostapd_set_sta_flags() so that both paths look the same to the driver.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -8563,6 +8563,21 @@
 			goto handle_ml;
 	}
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211R_AP
+	if (sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_FT) {
+		/*
+		 * Configure the PTK derived in the FT protocol before the
+		 * driver STA entry is marked authorized, i.e., in the same
+		 * order as after the 4-way handshake. The driver STA entry
+		 * exists at this point (it was added or updated when the
+		 * (Re)Association Response frame was sent), so the earlier
+		 * attempt from the FT authentication that could not be
+		 * completed is retried here.
+		 */
+		wpa_auth_sm_event(sta->wpa_sm, WPA_ASSOC_FT);
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211R_AP */
+
 	hostapd_set_sta_flags(hapd, sta);
 
 	if (!(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_WDS) && sta->pending_wds_enable) {
@@ -8591,9 +8606,7 @@
 			hostapd_set_wds_encryption(hapd, sta, ifname_wds);
 	}
 
-	if (sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_FT)
-		wpa_auth_sm_event(sta->wpa_sm, WPA_ASSOC_FT);
-	else
+	if (sta->auth_alg != WLAN_AUTH_FT)
 		wpa_auth_sm_event(sta->wpa_sm, WPA_ASSOC);
 	hapd->new_assoc_sta_cb(hapd, sta, !new_assoc);
 	ieee802_1x_notify_port_enabled(sta->eapol_sm, 1);
